Summary: Fantasy–Fiat Wizardry System
This is a fictional thought-experiment framework 
designed to explore mathematical structures by 
imaginatively "zeroing out" components of two core 
triads:

Core Concept

  SID (Geometry): Structure, Interaction, Dynamics
  PED (Field): Power, Evaluation, Dynamics

By selectively removing (zeroing) one or two 
components from each triad, you generate 6 patterns 
per triad × 6 patterns = 36 total "wizard regimes."

Key Mechanisms
SID Zero-Patterns (e.g., Zero Structure → 
structureless geometry, Zero Dynamics → frozen 
geometry)

PED Zero-Patterns (e.g., Zero Power → powerless 
evaluation, Zero Dynamics → frozen skeleton)

FFF (Fantasy-Fiat Function): A transformation operator 
that performs the "wizardry"—diagonalization, basis
twisting, invariant extraction, etc.—without exposing 
how it works.

Purpose
This is explicitly a sandbox for exploration, not a 
claim about physical reality. It lets you:

Isolate invariants
Suppress components to simplify equations
Test hypotheses in a constrained, enumerable space
Explore "forbidden" assumptions (like physics thought 
experiments with frictionless surfaces)
Critical boundary marker: All fantasy results remain 
fantasy until independently justified by the underlying 
technical framework.

Notation
Three equivalent notations express the 36 regimes: 
caret-underscore, Wizard-W, and Triple-F (FFF).

It's also designed as an RPG magic subsystem with 
spellcasting operators and a mana generator.

